# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party literature, guidance and reports: never committed.
#
# Copyrighted PDFs are not redistributed; 04.references/README.md records
# provenance and retrieval for each. Markdown conversions of copyrighted
# sources are excluded too: converting a format does not change the copyright.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
04.references/literature/
04.references/reports/
04.references/standards/

# macOS resource forks
._*
**/._*
.DS_Store
.Rproj.user

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw input data: NEVER committed.
#
# Large third-party data (imagery, LiDAR, model checkpoints) lives on the
# external drive; git carries only a manifest of provenance plus the small
# derived CSVs the manuscript actually cites. GitHub hard-rejects any file
# over 100 MB, so an accidental `git add 02.inputs` would wedge the repo.
#
# Everything under 02.inputs is ignored by default; the exceptions below
# re-admit the documentation, the scripts and the derived outputs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
02.inputs/**
!02.inputs/
!02.inputs/**/
!02.inputs/**/*.md
!02.inputs/**/*.R
!02.inputs/**/*.py

# Derived CSVs written by saved scripts ARE committed: they are the numbers
# the manuscript cites, under the rule that no figure may be quoted from
# code that was not saved.
!02.inputs/derived/**
!02.inputs/derived/*.csv

# The derived/** re-admission above would otherwise let macOS resource forks
# back in; re-exclude them last so the ._* rule wins.
02.inputs/**/._*

# The per-area Sentinel-1 samples (635 MB over 178 areas) and the per-fire
# samples of the archived wildfire draft (295 MB) are regenerable from the
# s1-samples chunk and Earth Engine; never committed.
02.inputs/derived/tile_samples/
02.inputs/derived/tile_samples_pre/
02.inputs/derived/landscape_tiles/
02.inputs/derived/fire_samples/

# The sits analysis cube is regenerable rasters split from the composites by
# the sits-cube-build manuscript chunk (~190 MB); never committed.
02.inputs/derived/sits_cube/

# Python bytecode and environments
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Quarto render sidecar: regenerable JS/CSS libraries.
01.manuscript/*_files/

# Private notes and working files, per the library convention. Unlike the
# sibling project, .gitignore itself IS tracked here.
/docs/
/tasks/
/05.tasks/
/attachments/
INDEX.md

!02.inputs/**/SHA256SUMS.txt
01.manuscript/Rplots.pdf
~$*.docx
**/~$*
01.manuscript/manuscript/

# Local state for the prose guard; regenerated with --record.
01.manuscript/_tools/.prose_guard.json

# Eval run reports. One CSV per run of 01.manuscript/_tools/eval.py, so the
# directory grows with every check rather than with every result. Nothing in
# the manuscript cites them and no check reads them; the state a later run
# compares against lives in 03.outputs/eval-baseline.json, which is committed.
03.outputs/eval/

# The rendered manuscript. Regenerated from the .qmd, which is the single
# source of truth, so a committed copy is only ever a stale one; the render
# that matters is the one the eval runs with --render.
01.manuscript/manuscript.html

# Radar block stacks and cube, regenerable from 05.scripts/14, 15 and 19; the cube alone is 437 MB
02.inputs/derived/s1_scene_cache_30m/
02.inputs/derived/s1_block_stack_30m*.npz
02.inputs/derived/s1_cube_30m/
02.inputs/derived/s1_cube/
02.inputs/derived/s1_reg_test/
.Rhistory

# Regenerable radar stores of the 10 m design (36 GB cube, 6 GB scene cache, two 5.5 GB
# block stacks), the set-aside 10 m statewide run, the 1 km read-back of the statewide
# asset (31 MB, rebuilt by the statewide-map chunk), the stand cell layers of the old
# design, the wildfire draft's chips and predictions, and stray render files. Added
# 2026-10-15 before the redraft commit so that none of them can reach GitHub.
02.inputs/derived/s1_blocks_10m/
02.inputs/derived/s1_blocks_10m_mtfiltered/
02.inputs/derived/s1_cube_10m/
02.inputs/derived/s1_scene_cache_10m/
02.inputs/derived/statewide_10m_run_*/
02.inputs/derived/*.tif
02.inputs/derived/*.gpkg
02.inputs/derived/stand_cells_static.csv
03.outputs/reference_chips/
03.outputs/fire_fold_predictions.csv
01.manuscript/_archive/*.html
Rplots.pdf

# The 90 m release package of the statewide map, built by the statewide-release chunk:
# the 180 download tiles (regenerable) and the two GeoTIFFs and the zip, which go to a
# GitHub release and not into git (the four-band file is about 1 GB). The README,
# licence, style and template beside them are committed. Added 2026-10-18.
02.inputs/derived/release_tiles/
03.outputs/release/*.tif
03.outputs/release/*.zip

# Word copies of the author's edits, the submission folder's duplicates of the renders and
# the journal's TIFF figures are build products that bloat the history; the renders in
# 01.manuscript and the PNG figures the README shows are the committed copies. Added 2026-10-19.
01.manuscript/_archive/*.docx
03.outputs/submission/*.docx
03.outputs/submission/*.tif
03.outputs/figures/*.tif
/cover_letter.docx
01.manuscript/cover_letter/
